00:07:40.039 --> 00:07:45.039
Teams are refining the 2029 encounter plan while the probe runs on its second extension.

00:07:45.039 --> 00:07:50.019
That extra time lets it watch other near-earth asteroids before the close pass at a

00:07:50.019 --> 00:07:50.539
poffis.

00:07:51.564 --> 00:07:55.524
Laboratory tests show water molecules rearranging into new shapes under the

00:07:55.524 --> 00:08:00.584
pressures and temperatures inside ice giants and super-earths, according to Fizz.org.

00:08:01.024 --> 00:08:05.064
The new bonding changes density, conductivity, and optical properties.

00:08:05.664 --> 00:08:08.484
Those phases feed interior models of distant worlds.

00:08:09.024 --> 00:08:12.884
The experiments produce structures never seen under conditions at Earth's surface.

